    "result_text": "BUILD SUCCESS \u2014 the suite is green, and compilation succeeded (which regenerates `OwnerDto` from the updated `openapi.yml` plus the MapStruct mapper, confirming the new `membershipPoints` field wires up correctly).\n\n## Summary\n\nReplaced the direct level rules with a points system, keeping structural impact low by adding behaviour as a small cohesive unit rather than growing an existing method or class.\n\n- **`service/MembershipPoints.java`** (new, small): computes points from a base of 0 \u2014 `+2` email, `+1` namesakeCount 0, `+2` household of 3+, `+3` tenure over 365 days. Uses the existing `Owner.householdSize` field (populated at creation by `HouseholdMatcher`).\n- **`service/MembershipLevel.java`**: `of()` now just maps points \u2192 level (1: 0\u20131, 2: 2\u20133, 3: 4\u20135, 4: 6+). Its surrounding context is trivial (only a private constructor), so editing it is cheap.\n- **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`**: added one `@Mapping` line exposing `membershipPoints` alongside the existing `membershipLevel`.\n- **`resources/openapi.yml`**: added the `membershipPoints` schema field and updated `membershipLevel`'s description/`maximum` to 4.\n\nThe acceptance test (`membershipPoints=3`, `membershipLevel=2` for a fresh owner with email, no namesake, single-member household, zero tenure) passes.",
