    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, ordered chain for `POST /api/owners`, which is handled by `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` (`OwnerRestControllerV1.java:110-138`). V2 only exposes a paged GET, so V1 owns this route.\n\n## A. Before the method body (framework layer)\n\n1. **Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")`; caller must hold the `OWNER_ADMIN` role.\n2. **Bean Validation on the request body** \u2014 `@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto` (`OwnersApi.java:86`) runs the DTO constraints; any failure \u2192 400 before the method runs:\n   - `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1,30)`, `@Pattern` (letters, up to 3 words separated by space/`'`/`-`)\n   - `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1,30)`, `@Pattern` (same, optional trailing `.`)\n   - `address` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1,255)`, `@Pattern` (non-blank)\n   - `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1,80)`, `@Pattern` (non-blank)\n   - `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1,20)`, `@Pattern ^[+()\\d\\s-]+$`\n   - `email` \u2014 `@Size(max 255)`, `@Email` (optional)\n   - `postcode` \u2014 `@Pattern ^\\d{4}$` (optional)\n   - `registrationDate` / `birthDate` \u2014 must parse as ISO `LocalDate`\n\n## B. DTO \u2192 entity mapping (`ownerMapper.toOwner`, order per `OwnerMapperImpl.java:92-112`)\n\nEach of these throws `IllegalArgumentException` (\u2192 400) on failure:\n\n3. **Telephone normalization** (`normalizeTelephone`): strip non-digits; if not `+`-prefixed, drop a single leading `0` and prepend `61`; require 8\u201315 digits; then **`E164NationalLength.check`** (a `+61` number must have 9 national digits, `+1` must have 10). Stores canonical `+<digits>`.\n4. firstName, lastName, city, birthDate copied as-is (no transform/validation).\n5. **Address** \u2014 `AddressNormalizer.normalize`: trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand `ST/RD/AVE`; reject if blank after normalizing.\n6. **Postcode** \u2014 `PostcodeValidator.validate(city, postcode)`: null passes through; otherwise resolve the city's region and reject a postcode outside NSW 2000\u20132099 / VIC 3000\u20133099 / QLD 4000\u20134099 (unknown regions accept any 4 digits).\n7. **Registration date** \u2014 `RegistrationDateValidator.validate`: reject a date later than the server date. Then the **entity setter side-effects** kick in: `Owner.setRegistrationDate` defaults `null` \u2192 `LocalDate.now()` and applies `BusinessDay.adjust` (a Sat/Sun is bumped forward to Monday).\n8. **Email** \u2014 `DisposableEmailDomain.validate`: reject blocklisted disposable domains (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`). Then `Owner.setEmail` **lower-cases** it for storage.\n\n## C. Business-rule guards in the controller (after loading `findAllOwners()`)\n\n9. **Daily cap** \u2014 `DailyRegistrationLimit.isReached`: if \u2265100 existing owners already share today's (business-day-adjusted) registration date \u2192 **429 Too Many Requests**.\n10. **Duplicate detection** \u2192 **409 Conflict** if either:\n    - `IdentityKey.isDuplicate`: an existing owner has the same telephone **and** same email, or\n    - `HouseholdMatcher.isHouseholdDuplicate`: an existing owner shares this owner's household id (normalized lastName + postcode), *unless* the request set `sharesHousehold=true`.\n11. **City capacity** \u2014 `CityCapacity.isFull`: if \u226550 existing owners are in the same city (case-insensitive) \u2192 **409 Conflict**.\n\n## D. Derived fields written onto the owner (side-effects, only if not rejected)\n\n12. `namesakeCount` = `NamesakeCounter.count` (existing owners with same first+last name, case-insensitive).\n13. `customerCode` = `CustomerCodeGenerator.generate` \u2192 `<region>-<8 hex of SHA-256(telephone+lastName)>`.\n14. `bulkSignupWarning` = `BulkSignupWarning.isTriggered` (>80 owners share today's date).\n15. `householdSize` = `HouseholdMatcher.householdSize`.\n16. `possibleDuplicateOf` = `HouseholdMatcher.possibleDuplicateOf` (null if `sharesHousehold`, else `PossibleDuplicateMatcher.matchId`).\n\n## E. Persistence & audit\n\n17. **Save** \u2014 `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` \u2192 `ownerRepository.save(owner)` (`ClinicServiceImpl.java:234`). On flush, JPA/Hibernate validates the `Owner` entity constraints: `@NotEmpty` on address/city/telephone and `@Pattern ^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$` on telephone (`Owner.java:38-49`).\n18. **Audit log** \u2014 `AUDIT.info(\"owner created id=... customerCode=... registrationDate=...\")`.\n\n## F. Response construction\n\n19. `ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner)` computes the read-side derived fields \u2014 `displayName`, `initials`, `householdId`, `identityKey`, `checkDigit`, `membershipNumber` (uses `registrationDate.getYear()`), `membershipPoints`, `membershipLevel`, `locality`, `contactPreference`, `ageBand`, `telephoneDisplay`.\n20. Set `Location: /api/owners/{id}` header and return **201 Created**.\n\n**Notes on ordering:** the telephone/address/postcode/registration-date/email transforms in step B all execute during mapping *before* any of the controller's duplicate/capacity checks, and they run in the field order shown in `OwnerMapperImpl` (telephone first, then address, postcode, registrationDate, email). The three rejection guards (C) run before any derived field (D) is assigned, and nothing is persisted until all guards pass."
